{"result":"{
  "id": "18206",
  "key": "SFCC-123",
  "summary": "Spike: Contentful Integration Technical Design & Content Model",
  "description": "**Objective**\n\nUnderstand the Contentful integration architecture, define the content models required for SFCC, and identify what the Accenture squad needs to build on the SFCC side before the dedicated Contentful squad comes onboard.\n\n**Background**\n\nContentful is the CMS for Zimmermann's storefront content (page layouts, editorial, imagery, assets, navigation, and merchandising). A separate Contentful SOW and squad are incoming — they will own the full Contentful setup. However, there is significant SFCC-side work required to integrate with Contentful via MRT, and the team needs an early understanding of the content model structure and integration pattern before that squad arrives.\n\nTim has confirmed the team needs to set up layouts and content models, and understand the integration deeply enough to build the SFCC-side connection correctly.\n\n**Tasks**\n\n- Document the Contentful → MRT → SFCC integration pattern and data flow\n- Identify which content types are required in Contentful for Sprint 1 and 2 (e.g. page layouts, content slots, editorial components)\n- Define what the SFCC side needs to consume from Contentful: which APIs, which content model fields, what rendering logic\n- Identify locale configuration requirements in Contentful aligned to the 8 storefronts\n- Clarify the handoff boundary: what Accenture builds vs what the incoming Contentful squad owns\n- Flag any blockers or dependencies that need to be resolved before the Contentful squad onboards\n\n**Definition of Done**\n\nA technical design document is produced covering the Contentful integration architecture, content model requirements, locale setup, and SFCC-side build scope — ready to be shared with the incoming Contentful squad as a briefing artefact.",
