{"result":"{
  "metadata": {
    "id": "320602113",
    "title": "MuleSoft Integration — Open Questions for SFCC / PWA Design",
    "type": "page",
    "created": "",
    "updated": "",
    "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/320602113",
    "space": {
      "key": "SFCC",
      "name": "Adobe SFCC"
    },
    "version": 21,
    "attachments": [],
    "content": {
      "value": "This page consolidates all open questions for the MuleSoft team relevant to the Zimmermann SFCC / PWA integration design. Where an answer is already known from existing documentation, it is pre-filled and flagged for **confirmation only**. Questions that are not MuleSoft's responsibility have been removed.\n\nCovers both **data sync (inbound to SFCC)** and **real-time API calls (SFCC/PWA → MuleSoft)**.\n\n**Legend:** - ✅ **Known** — answer pre-filled from existing documentation; MuleSoft to confirm - ❓ **Unknown** — no answer exists in any page; MuleSoft to answer\n\n> **Context for Sections 2, 3, and 4:** The SFCC integration for product, price, and inventory has not been built yet. MuleSoft's current integration experience is with Magento. These questions focus on understanding the current Magento process so the SFCC team can determine the right integration approach for each domain.\n\n---\n\n1-general--architecture1. General / Architecture\n------------------------------------------------\n\n| # | Domain | Question | What we need | Priority | Response |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| G1 | Architecture | Confirm MuleSoft API base URL pattern per environment. | ✅ Known: Dev → `https://mw.staging.zimmermann.com/{api-name}-dev/api/`, QA → `{api-name}-qa/api/`, Prod → `https://mw.staging.zimmermann.com/{api-name}/api/`. Confirm: is the production base domain `mw.zimmermann.com` (not `mw.staging.zimmermann.com`) and is UAT a separate environment with its own pattern? | P0 |  |\n| G2 | Auth | Confirm auth mechanism for SFCC → MuleSoft real-time API calls. | ✅ Known: client credentials (client\\_id / client\\_secret) via Mule secure property placeholder. Confirm: are credentials issued per-environment (separate Dev / QA / Prod sets)? | P0 |  |\n| G3 | Performance | What is the MuleSoft rate limit per API per environment? | ❓ The SFCC PWA spikes heavily on product launches and sales — Find In Store, order history, and checkout all make real-time MuleSoft calls. SFCC needs to know the limit to design client-side back-off or caching. | P0 |  |\n| G6 | Architecture | The SFCC team has access to Anypoint Exchange but the volume of specs makes it hard to identify which are relevant. | ❓ Please provide the specific Anypoint Exchange API spec names (or direct links) for the following touchpoints: customer outbound sync, order creation, order history & returns, and Find In Store. | P0 |  |\n\n---\n\n2-product-sync-ap21--mulesoft--sfcc2. Product Sync (AP21 → MuleSoft → SFCC)\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n| # | Domain | Question | What we need | Priority | Response |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| P-M1a | Product Sync | What format does AP21 output for the product feed — XML, JSON, CSV, or another format? | ❓ Tells us whether MuleSoft already has an AP21 product connector reusable for SFCC. | P0 |  |\n| P-M1b | Product Sync | How is the AP21 product feed delivered to Magento — SFTP drop, API call, direct DB write, or another method? | ❓ | P0 |  |\n| P-M1c | Product Sync | Does MuleSoft sit in the AP21 → Magento product path today, or is it a direct integration? | ❓ | P0 |  |\n| P-M2a | Product Sync | Does AP21 send the full product catalogue each run, or only products changed since the last export? | ❓ Volume and change detection capability are key inputs to the SFCC integration approach. | P0 |  |\n| P-M2b | Product Sync | If delta — what is the change signal AP21 uses (last-modified timestamp, event, flag)? | ❓ | P0 |  |\n| P-M2c | Product Sync | What is the approximate catalogue volume — number of master styles and total variant SKUs in the current export? | ❓ | P0 |  |\n| P-M3a | Product Sync | Is the AP21 → Magento product feed triggered on a schedule, on AP21 product publish/update event, or both? If scheduled — what is the interval? | ❓ Sets the expected freshness SLA for SFCC. | P0 |  |\n| P-M3b | Product Sync | How quickly does a product change in AP21 become live on Magento today — minutes, hours, or overnight? | ❓ | P0 |  |\n| P-M4 | Product Sync | When a product is archived or suppressed in AP21, how does Magento know to take it offline — does AP21 send an explicit status flag, or is the product simply absent from the next feed? | ❓ SFCC merge mode will keep a product live indefinitely if it is merely absent — an explicit offline signal is required. | P0 |  |\n| P-M5a | Product Sync | Does MuleSoft transform the AP21 product payload before Magento receives it, or does Magento consume the raw AP21 format directly? | ❓ For SFCC, MuleSoft will need to produce a new output format — understanding re-use potential of the current mapping. | P0 |  |\n| P-M5b | Product Sync | If MuleSoft transforms — where is the field mapping defined (MuleSoft DataWeave, a config file, or a mapping table)? | ❓ | P0 |  |\n| P-M6 | Error Handling | Does the MuleSoft failure alert for the product feed include individual failed product IDs, or only a job-level notification? | ✅ Known: 3 retries, automated email alert on failure. Confirm: per-product IDs or job-level only? | P1 |  |\n\n---\n\n3-price-sync-ap21--mulesoft--sfcc3. Price Sync (AP21 → MuleSoft → SFCC)\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n| # | Domain | Question | What we need | Priority | Response |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| PR-M1a | Price Sync | Does AP21 send price data bundled with the product export, or as a separate price-only feed? | ❓ Determines whether MuleSoft owns price sync for SFCC or whether it needs to be scoped as new work. | P0 |  |\n| PR-M1b | Price Sync | Does MuleSoft currently process or transform AP21 price data before Magento receives it, or is it a direct AP21 → Magento connection? | ❓ | P0 |  |\n| PR-M2a | Price Sync | Are price updates sent on the same schedule as product updates, or does AP21 emit a separate price change event? | ❓ Informs whether SFCC pricebook import needs a frequent schedule or a seasonal trigger. | P1 |  |\n| PR-M2b | Price Sync | Approximately how often do prices change in AP21 — daily, weekly, or on seasonal sale events only? | ❓ | P1 |  |\n| PR-M3a | Price Sync | Does AP21 have a dedicated `special_price` field, a date-ranged sale flag, or a separate sale price record per product? | ❓ Critical for SFCC: sale pricebook entries are not auto-removed — MuleSoft must send an explicit removal signal. | P0 |  |\n| PR-M3b | Price Sync | When a sale ends, does AP21 explicitly clear the sale price, or does it simply stop sending it? | ❓ | P0 |  |\n| PR-M3c | Price Sync | How does Magento currently handle sale price removal — does it rely on an explicit AP21 signal or does it expire sale prices by date? | ❓ | P0 |  |\n\n---\n\n4-inventory-sync--mulesoft--sfcc4. Inventory Sync (→ MuleSoft → SFCC)\n---------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n> **Note:** The current MuleSoft `inventory-sync-prc-api` covers GB, AU, and US sourced from NewStore. The source system for **ZimmermannEU (domestic)**, **ZimmermannEUIntl**, **ZimmermannHK**, and **ZimmermannME** is unconfirmed — it may be AP21 directly, NewStore, or a shared regional pool. This must be established before any SFCC inventory design for those sites can proceed.\n\n| # | Domain | Question | What we need | Priority | Response |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| I-M1a | Inventory Sync | Does MuleSoft currently push inventory to Magento on the same 15-minute schedule as the NewStore sync, or is the Magento inventory update a different process? | ❓ Determines how much of the existing MuleSoft inventory flow can be reused for SFCC. | P0 |  |\n| I-M1b | Inventory Sync | What format does Magento receive inventory in — API call per SKU, batch file, or direct DB update? | ❓ | P0 |  |\n| I-M1c | Inventory Sync | Does MuleSoft sit in the Magento inventory path today, or does NewStore push to Magento directly? | ❓ | P0 |  |\n| I-M2 | Inventory Sync | Does the current Magento inventory update include per-location stock levels (DC + boutique), or is it an aggregated available quantity per SKU across all locations? | ❓ SFCC inventory lists store a single qty per SKU per list — if MuleSoft currently sends location-level detail, it will need to aggregate before writing to SFCC. | P0 |  |\n| I-M3 | Inventory Sync | When a SKU goes OOS in NewStore, does MuleSoft send qty=0 to Magento, or is the record removed entirely from the inventory feed? | ❓ A missing inventory record in SFCC defaults to the `default-instock` setting on the inventory list — sending qty=0 explicitly is the safe approach. | P1 |  |\n| I-M4a | Inventory Sync | For ZimmermannEU domestic — does NewStore manage EU fulfilment locations, or is EU stock held and managed in AP21 only? | ❓ Determines whether the existing `inventory-sync-prc-api` can be extended or whether a new AP21 → SFCC inventory flow is required for EU. | P0 |  |\n| I-M4b | Inventory Sync | For ZimmermannEUIntl, ZimmermannHK, ZimmermannME — are these Global-e sites fulfilling from a shared EU or AU stock pool, or from dedicated regional locations? | ❓ | P0 |  |\n| I-M4c | Inventory Sync | Which system (NewStore or AP21) is the source of available inventory quantities for ZimmermannEU, ZimmermannEUIntl, ZimmermannHK, and ZimmermannME? | ❓ | P0 |  |\n| I-M5 | Inventory Sync | Has MuleSoft updated `inventory-sync-prc-api` to target legacy SFCC inventory lists (`inventory_m_au`, `inventory_m_uk`, `inventory_m_us`) rather than OCI endpoints? | ✅ Known: Zimmermann uses legacy SFCC inventory lists, not OCI. The INT register (INT-013) incorrectly references SFCC OCI API. Confirm the update has been made. | P0 |  |\n| I-M6a | Inventory Sync | Does NewStore include a buffer stock level as a separate field in the inventory payload (e.g. `buffer_qty`, `safety_stock`, or similar), distinct from the raw on-hand quantity? | ❓ To correctly calculate online available stock for SFCC, we need to know whether NewStore provides buffer stock as an explicit field or whether it is embedded in the ATP quantity. If NewStore surfaces buffer separately, MuleSoft can subtract it from the on-hand quantity before writing to SFCC — ensuring the SFCC `allocation` value reflects true online-available stock rather than total physical stock. | P0 |  |\n| I-M6b | Inventory Sync | If NewStore provides a buffer stock field — can MuleSoft calculate `online available stock = on-hand qty − buffer qty` and write the result as the `allocation` value in the SFCC inventory record? | ❓ This calculation must happen in MuleSoft before the SFCC inventory write. If MuleSoft passes raw on-hand quantity without buffer deduction, SFCC will oversell against stock that is physically reserved. | P0 |  |\n| I-M6c | Inventory Sync | If NewStore does not provide a buffer stock field — is the ATP (Available-to-Promise) quantity NewStore exposes already net of buffer, or does the buffer need to be applied in SFCC availability configuration? | ❓ Confirm which side owns the buffer calculation so there is no double-deduction or gap. | P0 |  |\n| I-M7 | Inventory Sync | Which concession stores are excluded from AU and US inventory sync, and who is responsible for maintaining the exclusion list when stores are added or removed? | ❓ | P1 |  |\n| I-M8 | Multi-region | For the 15-minute sync across GB, AU, US — does MuleSoft run parallel scheduler instances per region or a single sequential flow? If sequential, what is the total wall-clock time per run? | ❓ Sequential runs risk overlap at 15-minute intervals under load. | P1 |  |\n\n---\n\n5-orders-sfcc--mulesoft--newstore--realtime5. Orders (SFCC → MuleSoft → NewStore) — Real-Time\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n| # | Domain | Question | What we need | Priority | Response |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| O2 | Orders | What fields does `orders-prc-api` return to SFCC on successful order creation in NewStore? | ❓ SFCC requires at minimum: NewStore order ID (e.g. ZX00000339), order status, and any error details. Confirm: does NewStore use the SFCC order ID, or does it generate its own? | P0 |  |\n| O3 | Orders | What happens if `orders-prc-api` does not respond within 30 seconds — does MuleSoft have an async fallback or does the checkout fail? | ❓ A customer-charged-but-not-fulfilled scenario must be mitigated. | P0 |  |\n| O4a | Orders | Does MuleSoft perform a stock check against NewStore before creating the order? | ❓ | P0 |  |\n| O4b | Orders | If NewStore rejects due to OOS post-checkout, how does MuleSoft notify SFCC? | ❓ | P0 |  |\n| O5 | Orders | Does MuleSoft read the SFCC site ID from the order payload to determine NewStore fulfilment routing (e.g. ZimmermannUK → UK NewStore, ZimmermannAU → AU NewStore)? | ✅ Known: SFCC sends orderId → MuleSoft fetches full order. Confirm site routing behaviour. | P0 |  |\n| O6a | Orders | Is the NewStore order ID returned to SFCC for storage after order creation? | ✅ Known: NewStore uses ZX-prefix format (e.g. ZX00000339). Confirm it is returned in the response. | P0 |  |\n| O6b | Orders | How does `orders-prc-api` resolve the SFCC customer ID to NewStore customer orders for My Account reconciliation? | ❓ | P0 |  |\n| O7 | Orders | Is the rewards split calculation (0-value orders) performed in MuleSoft before sending to NewStore, or does SFCC send pre-calculated values? | ✅ Known: rewards split formula documented in order TSD. Confirm which side calculates. | P1 |  |\n\n---\n\n6-order-history--returns-sfccpwa--mulesoft--realtime6. Order History & Returns (SFCC/PWA → MuleSoft) — Real-Time\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n| # | Domain | Question | What we need | Priority | Response |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| OH1 | Order History | What are the SFCC-context endpoint names and production URLs for order list, order detail, and returns? | ✅ Known: current URLs use `magento-exp-api-dev` (e.g. `https://mw.staging.zimmermann.com/magento-exp-api-dev/api/orders`). Confirm the renamed SFCC endpoints — PWA My Account development is blocked without these. | P0 |  |\n| OH2 | Order History | What is the maximum `count` per request on the order history endpoint, and what is the default if omitted? | ✅ Known: `offset` and `count` params supported. Confirm the limit. | P1 |  |\n| OH4 | Returns | Is the `/returns` endpoint live in MuleSoft and what is the response schema? | ✅ Known: separate `GET /returns?customer_id={id}` endpoint documented. Confirm it is live and provide schema — return ID, status, items, refund amount. | P1 |  |\n| OH5 | Customer | Is the SFCC customer ID stored in NewStore at order creation time, or does MuleSoft maintain a cross-reference (e.g. Anypoint Object Store)? | ❓ Required for My Account order history resolution. | P0 |  |",
      "format": "markdown"
    },
