spect | Detail |\n| --- | --- |\n| Purpose | Editorial content: hero banners, collection pages, lookbook, rich PDP copy |\n| Rendering | PWA Kit fetches content at runtime via Contentful Delivery API |\n| Scope | Non-product content; all product data remains in SFCC catalogue sourced from AP21 via MuleSoft |\n\n---\n\n7-multilocale-product-content7. Multi-Locale Product Content\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\n| Site | Locales | Language Tags |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ZimmermannAU | en | `x-default`, `en` |\n| ZimmermannUK | en, en\\_GB | `x-default`, `en`, `en-GB` |\n| ZimmermannUS | en, en\\_US | `x-default`, `en`, `en-US` |\n| ZimmermannUSIntl | en, en\\_US | `x-default`, `en`, `en-US` |\n| ZimmermannEU | en, en\\_GB, fr, it, es | `x-default`, `en`, `fr`, `it`, `es` |\n| ZimmermannEUIntl | en, en\\_CH | `x-default`, `en`, `en-CH` |\n| ZimmermannHK | en, en\\_HK | `x-default`, `en`, `en-HK` |\n| ZimmermannME | en, en\\_AE | `x-default`, `en`, `en-AE` |\n\nProduct XML attributes use `xml:lang` for each locale. The `x-default` value is always English.\n\n---\n\n8-product-display-page-pdp--mulesoft-touchpoints8. Product Display Page (PDP) — MuleSoft Touchpoints\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nMuleSoft is the integration layer for the product import pipeline (see Section 4.2). In addition, the PDP has two further MuleSoft-dependent runtime features:\n\n| Feature | API | Detail |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Find In Store / Boutique Stock | `product-availibility-prc-api` | Real-time store stock availability shown on PDP |\n| Real-time DC stock check | [TBC] | Online availability from NewStore fulfilment groups |\n\n---\n\n9-key-design-decisions9. Key Design Decisions\n---------------------------------------------\n\n| Decision | Choice | Rationale |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Product source of truth | AP21 | AP21 is the ERP and master for all product data |\n| Product integration layer | MuleSoft | Consistent with Zimmermann integration platform; MuleSoft handles AP21 event consumption, transformation, and SFCC delivery |\n| Product imagery | Loaded directly into SFCC | No external DAM or Cloudinary in the pipeline; images stored in SFCC static content library |\n| Catalogue structure | One master + eight storefront catalogues | SFCC best practice for multi-site |\n| Editorial content | Contentful | Decouples editorial from product data; supports headless PWA pattern |\n| Category positions | Explicit `<position>` elements per category | Ensures nav order matches Figma design across all sites |\n| USIntl separate storefront catalogue | `zimmermann-us-intl-storefront-catalog` | Allows independent category assignment for Global-e international customers |\n\n---\n\n10-open-items10. Open Items\n---------------------------\n\n| # | Item | Owner | Status |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Confirm MuleSoft delivery mechanism to SFCC — OCAPI Data API vs SFTP + import job; confirm trigger (event-driven vs scheduled batch) | Integration Lead / MuleSoft team | Open |\n| 2 | Confirm product attribute set required for SFCC | Zimmermann Merch team | **Closed** — see [TSD: Product — SFCC Product Attributes](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/312377345) |\n| 3 | Define Contentful content model and connector customisation scope | Frontend Dev | Open |\n| 4 | Product imagery source and pipeline | Zimmermann Digital | **Closed** — images loaded directly into SFCC static content library; no Cloudinary or external DAM in pipeline |\n| 5 | Confirm whether ZimmermannUSIntl storefront catalogue requires different category structure or promotions vs ZimmermannUS | Zimmermann US Merch | Open |\n| 6 | Confirm Magento store\\_id → SFCC site mapping for stores 6, 9, 12, 18, 19, 22, 25, 28, 35, 38, 40, 43 | Integration Lead | Open |\n\n---\n\n11-product-attribute-mapping11. Product Attribute Mapping\n---------------------------------------------------------\n\nThe full AP21 → MuleSoft → SFCC product attribute mapping (system attributes, custom attributes, pricebook conventions, and ignored fields) has been extracted to a dedicated page:\n\n➡️ **[TSD: Product — SFCC Product Attributes](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/312377345)**\n\nThat page is derived from the Magento product CSV export (`sfccexport.csv`) and verified against the Magento staging REST API. The conversion script lives at `scripts/magento-to-sfcc.js` in the `zimmermann-sfccworkplace` repository.",
      "format": "markdown"
    },
    "page_width": "fixed-width"
  }
}"}

